                           '<b>00:00</b>. The session stays open. <b>Cancel countdown</b>, Esc or '
                           'closing the window cancels the power action. You can explicitly choose '
                           '<b>Restart now</b> or <b>Shut down now</b> to skip the remaining '
                           'time.</li><li>Only after expiry or that explicit choice does Bitcoin '
                           'Core close, the clipboard clear and the RAM session end. If Core '
                           'cannot close, the power action stops and the workspace remains '
                           'available.</li></ol>\n'
                           '<p><b>No passphrases are requested during shutdown or restart.</b> '
                           'These are warnings and your confirmations, not backup verification. '
                           'Verification still occurs when creating a backup; test recovery before '
                           'relying on it. Copies saved on external media remain after shutdown. '
                           'Power loss can end the session without warnings. Volatile storage is '
                           'not protection from live RAM acquisition or a compromised '
                           'computer.</p>\n',
 'Sign a PSBT offline': '\n'
                        '<h2>Sign a PSBT offline</h2>\n'
                        '<ol><li>Use Files to copy the unsigned PSBT from removable media into '
                        '<b>Private Workspace</b>, then open it in Bitcoin Core. Core can also '
                        'read the connected USB directly.</li><li>Independently check the '
                        'recipients, amounts, fee, change and wallet details before '
                        'signing.</li><li>Sign with the intended wallet. If its private keys are '
                        'encrypted, supply the separate Core wallet passphrase.</li><li>Save the '
                        'signed PSBT in <b>Private Workspace</b>. Core’s USB view is '
                        'read-only.</li><li>Use <b>Files</b> to copy only the signed PSBT to the '
                        'intended transfer medium.</li><li>Broadcast from the separate online '
                        'coordinator. The Vault stays offline.</li></ol>\n'
                        '<p>Mounted drives appear in the chooser sidebar. If a drive was connected '
                        'while the chooser was open, reopen that chooser or select <b>USB '
                        'Media</b>. Keep the original signing wallet and decrypted wallet backups '
                        'in the offline environment.</p>\n',
 'Recovery / inheritance': '\n'
                           '<h2>Recovery / inheritance</h2><p>Keep secret-free instructions '
                           'outside the encrypted backup. Identify the backup copies, required '
                           'secret holders, compatible software and how an heir can obtain access. '
                           'Do not put the only recovery instructions inside the backup they '
                           'explain.</p>\n'
                           '<h3>With Vault</h3><ol><li>Open the encrypted backup.</li><li>Enter '
                           'every external passphrase in any order. Vault finds the passphrase for '
                           'the outermost remaining layer.</li><li>Recover into a new Private '
                           'Workspace folder.</li><li>For a wallet, use Bitcoin Core’s <b>File → '
                           'Restore Wallet</b> on the recovered wallet.dat. Check expected '
                           'addresses, labels and a signing test. If encrypted in Core, supply its '
                           'separate internal passphrase when signing.</li></ol>\n'
                           '<p>Current single-wallet backups recover directly to wallet.dat. '
                           'Grouped files and folders, and older TAR-based wallet backups, recover '
                           'their original files from a validated TAR package. Older Vault OCB '
                           'backups remain supported by Vault recovery.</p>\n'
                           '<h3>Without Vault</h3><p>Use GnuPG with AES-256 CFB and OpenPGP MDC '
                           'support, plus Bitcoin Core. TAR is needed for grouped or older '
                           'TAR-based backups, not for a current single-wallet backup. Test your '
                           'exact recovery software with a disposable backup before relying on it; '
                           'legacy OCB files need software that supports that profile.</p>\n'
                           '<p>Work on a trusted offline system in an owned mode-0700 <b>tmpfs</b> '
                           'directory with swap disabled and sufficient RAM. Do not use a '
                           'persistent Downloads folder. Use new output filenames. Let GnuPG '
                           'prompt interactively; never put secrets in shell arguments, '
                           'environment variables or a script.</p>\n'
                           '<h3>Example: two-layer single-wallet backup</h3>\n'
                           '<pre>umask 077\n'
                           'gpg --output inner.gpg --decrypt wallet.dat.gpg.gpg &amp;&amp;\n'
                           'gpg --output wallet.dat --decrypt inner.gpg</pre>\n'
                           '<p>Enter the outer passphrase first, then the inner passphrase. With '
                           'one layer, decrypt wallet.dat.gpg directly to wallet.dat. Restore the '
                           'recovered wallet through Bitcoin Core’s <b>File → Restore Wallet</b>. '
                           'There is no TAR extraction for this direct-wallet format.</p>\n'
                           '<h3>Example: grouped files in a TAR payload</h3>\n'
                           '<p>After opening the known GPG layers, the last GPG command writes '
                           '<b>payload.tar</b> instead of wallet.dat. Inspect its listing before '
                           'extracting into a new RAM directory:</p>\n'
                           '<pre>tar --list --file payload.tar</pre>\n'
                           '<p>After checking the listing, extract into a new RAM directory:</p>\n'
                           '<pre>mkdir recovered &amp;&amp;\n'
                           'tar --extract --file payload.tar --directory recovered --no-same-owner '
                           '--no-same-permissions</pre>\n'
                           '<p><b>Proceed only after every GPG command exits successfully without '
                           'authentication errors.</b> Failed commands may leave provisional '
                           'output; do not use it. Stock GPG does not advertise the total Vault '
                           'layer count. Keep that information in your recovery plan.</p>\n'
                           '<p>Reject absolute paths, parent traversal, links, devices and '
                           'unexpected files in a TAR listing. Do not extract an untrusted archive '
                           'blindly. Vault performs strict validation. An original GPG or TAR file '
                           'inside a package remains an original file; stop there rather than '
                           'recursively opening it.</p>\n'
                           '<p>Practice with disposable data and the intended holders. Keep '
                           'independent usable copies of every required secret. A missing required '
                           'layer secret cannot be bypassed by Vault, and losing a password '
                           'manager’s unlocking secret is another recovery dependency.</p>\n',
 'Decrypt Backup': '\n'
                   '<h2>Decrypt Encrypted Backup</h2>\n'
                   '<p>Open <b>Decrypt Backup</b> on Home, double-click a .gpg file in Files, or '
                   'choose <b>Decrypt Encrypted Backup</b> from its context menu.</p>\n'
                   '<ol><li>Enter the available backup passphrases, in any order. Use <b>+ Add '
                   'Passphrase</b> for additional secrets.</li><li>Choose a new recovery folder '
                   'name. Click <b>Decrypt Backup</b>.</li><li>Vault authenticates each layer and '
                   'recovers into <b>Private Workspace</b>. A current single-wallet backup becomes '
                   'wallet.dat; grouped or older TAR-based backups restore their original '
                   'filenames and folders.</li></ol>\n'
                   '<p>If a secret is missing or wrong, add or correct it and retry. Damage and '
                   'unsupported encryption can also cause a failure. Partial recovered data are '
                   'discarded on failure or cancellation. Existing files are never '
                   'overwritten.</p>\n'
                   '<p>For an ordinary GPG file made outside Vault, select <b>Recover one ordinary '
                   'GPG layer only</b>. This deliberately stops after one authenticated layer and '
                   'saves <b>recovered-file</b>; it does not guess whether your original data are '
                   'themselves encrypted. Rename or handle that file explicitly. Vault recognizes '
                   'a complete supported wallet.dat or a validated TAR payload. An original GPG '
                   'file inside a TAR package is preserved unchanged.</p>\n'
                   '<p>Recovered plaintext stays in verified RAM. It disappears when the session '
                   'ends unless you explicitly export it. A recovered file alone is not a verified '
                   'current-wallet export.</p>\n'}

SECTIONS['Watch-Only Wallet in Bitcoin Core'] = '''
<h2>Watch-Only Wallet in Bitcoin Core</h2>
<p><b>Vault holds the signing keys. Your online node watches, prepares transactions and broadcasts. Vault reviews and signs.</b></p>
<h3>Export from Vault</h3>
<ol><li>Open Bitcoin Core and select your signing wallet.</li>
<li>Choose <b>File → Export watch-only wallet</b>.</li>
<li>The save dialog starts in <b>Private Workspace</b>. Keep that location and save the public copy as <b>watch-only.dat</b>. Core writes only to checked RAM locations in Vault.</li>
<li>Use <b>Files</b> to copy <b>watch-only.dat</b> to your transfer USB. Check the filename so you transfer the exported public copy, never the original signing wallet.</li></ol>
<p>The wide sidebar also shows mounted USB drives. Core can read them but cannot save to them directly. If you connect a drive while the chooser is open, reopen the chooser or select <b>USB Media</b>.</p>
<h3>Restore on your online node</h3>
<ol><li>Use Bitcoin Core <b>32.1 or newer</b> on your online computer.</li>
<li>Choose <b>File → Restore Wallet</b>, select the exported <b>watch-only.dat</b> and give it a new wallet name.</li>
<li>Check that the restored wallet is watch-only. Independently compare a receiving address with the signing wallet in Vault before using it.</li></ol>
<p>The export is a native Bitcoin Core wallet database containing public descriptors, address book data and transactions, without private keys. It replaces Vault's former JSON export. No separate Vault export button or Node JSON importer is needed for this file.</p>
<h3>Privacy and backup</h3>
<p>This public copy reveals wallet addresses, labels and activity. Keep it private. To encrypt it for storage or transfer, select it in <b>Files → Create Encrypted Backup</b>. Decrypt that copy on a trusted computer before using Core's Restore Wallet.</p>
<p>A watch-only copy cannot sign or recover your signing keys. Keep a separate verified backup of the signing wallet using <b>Wallet Backup</b>. The original signing wallet and its decrypted backups must stay offline.</p>
<p>Files saved only in Private Workspace disappear when the session ends. Copy everything you want to keep to external media before shutdown or restart.</p>
<h3>Synchronization and signing</h3>
<p>An older wallet may need a historical rescan. A pruned node may no longer hold the required blocks; an incomplete scan is not a verified balance.</p>
<p>Prepare a PSBT on the online node. Before signing in Vault, independently check recipients, amounts, fee, change and wallet derivations. Return only the signed transaction to the online node for broadcast.</p>
'''


# Same chapter treatment as Node Guide. Shared artwork keeps its upstream
# license; application chapters use the same installed theme icons as Home.
ASSETS = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2] / 'share/core-vault'
SECTION_ICONS = {
    'Home & keyboard': ('', ('input-keyboard',), QStyle.SP_ComputerIcon),
    'Bitcoin Core': ('bitcoin-ui.png', (), QStyle.SP_ComputerIcon),
    'KeePassXC': ('', ('keepassxc',), QStyle.SP_FileDialogDetailedView),
    'Brasero': ('', ('org.gnome.Brasero', 'brasero', 'media-optical'), QStyle.SP_DriveCDIcon),
    'Print & Labels': ('icons/print-labels.png', (), QStyle.SP_FileDialogDetailedView),
    'Files': ('', ('org.xfce.thunar', 'system-file-manager', 'folder'), QStyle.SP_DirIcon),
    'Editor': ('', ('org.xfce.mousepad', 'accessories-text-editor'), QStyle.SP_FileIcon),
    'Terminal': ('', ('org.xfce.terminal', 'utilities-terminal'), QStyle.SP_ComputerIcon),
    'Private Workspace': ('', ('folder-locked', 'folder'), QStyle.SP_DirIcon),
    'USB & optical media': ('', ('drive-removable-media-usb', 'drive-removable-media'), QStyle.SP_DriveHDIcon),
    'Create & encrypt a wallet': ('bitcoin-ui.png', (), QStyle.SP_ComputerIcon),
    'Generate a passphrase': ('', ('keepassxc',), QStyle.SP_FileDialogDetailedView),
    'Encryption security levels': ('icons/decrypt-backup.png', (), QStyle.SP_DriveHDIcon),
    'Backup & verify': ('icons/settings-chain-backup.png', (), QStyle.SP_DialogSaveButton),
    'Finish Private Session': ('icons/system-shutdown.png', (), QStyle.SP_DialogCloseButton),
    'Sign a PSBT offline': ('icons/settings-chain-backup.png', (), QStyle.SP_DialogSaveButton),
    'Recovery / inheritance': ('icons/settings-chain-import.png', (), QStyle.SP_DialogOpenButton),
    'Decrypt Backup': ('icons/decrypt-backup.png', (), QStyle.SP_DriveHDIcon),
    'Watch-Only Wallet in Bitcoin Core': ('bitcoin-ui.png', (), QStyle.SP_ComputerIcon),
}


def configure_icon_theme():
    # Match Home/Node application icons even when a minimal Qt platform theme
    # supplies no filesystem search paths (for example offscreen previews).
    paths = [str(ASSETS.parent / 'icons'), '/usr/share/icons', '/usr/local/share/icons',
             *QIcon.themeSearchPaths()]
    QIcon.setThemeSearchPaths(list(dict.fromkeys(paths)))
    QIcon.setThemeName('Adwaita')
    QIcon.setFallbackThemeName('hicolor')


def chapter_icon(section, style):
    if section in ('KeePassXC', 'Generate a passphrase'):
        for path in (Path('/opt/keepassxc/current/upstream-icon.png'),
                     ASSETS.parent / 'icons/hicolor/256x256/apps/keepassxc.png'):
            if path.is_file():
                return QIcon(str(path))
    bundled, names, fallback = SECTION_ICONS[section]
    if bundled:
        icon = QIcon(str(ASSETS / bundled))
        if not icon.isNull():
            return icon
    for name in names:
        icon = QIcon.fromTheme(name)
        if not icon.isNull():
            return icon
    return style.standardIcon(fallback)


class Guide(QWidget):
    def __init__(self):
        super().__init__()
        configure_icon_theme()
        self.setWindowTitle('Vault Guide')
        self.setWindowIcon(QIcon(str(ASSETS / 'bitcoin-ui.png')))
        self.resize(1180, 760)
        self.setStyleSheet(STYLE)
        self.layer_count = 1
        self.render_key = None
        self._render_timer = QTimer(self)
        self._render_timer.setSingleShot(True)
        self._render_timer.timeout.connect(self.render_section)
        outer = QVBoxLayout(self)
        outer.setContentsMargins(20, 16, 20, 20)
        outer.setSpacing(10)
        title = QLabel('Vault Guide')
        title.setObjectName('Title')
        outer.addWidget(title)
        sub = QLabel('Offline guidance for Bitcoin custody workflows and Vault tools.')
        sub.setObjectName('Subtitle')
        sub.setFont(UI_FONT)
        sub.setWordWrap(True)
        outer.addWidget(sub)
        self.section_picker = QComboBox()
        self.section_picker.setFont(UI_FONT)
        self.section_picker.setAccessibleName('Guide chapter')
        self.section_picker.addItems(list(SECTIONS))
        self.section_picker.hide()
        outer.addWidget(self.section_picker)
        body = QHBoxLayout()
        body.setSpacing(16)
        self.nav = QListWidget()
        self.nav.setFont(UI_FONT)
        self.nav.setFixedWidth(320)
        self.nav.setWordWrap(True)
        self.nav.setHorizontalScrollBarPolicy(Qt.ScrollBarAlwaysOff)
        self.nav.setTextElideMode(Qt.ElideNone)
        self.nav.viewport().installEventFilter(self)
        self.nav.setAccessibleName('Guide chapters')
        self.nav.addItems(list(SECTIONS))
        self.nav.setIconSize(QSize(26, 26))
        self.section_picker.setIconSize(QSize(26, 26))
        for row, section in enumerate(SECTIONS):
            icon = chapter_icon(section, self.style())
            self.nav.item(row).setIcon(icon)
            self.section_picker.setItemIcon(row, icon)
        self.viewer = QTextBrowser()
        self.viewer.setAccessibleName('Guide chapter and illustration description')
        self.viewer.viewport().installEventFilter(self)
        self.viewer.setSearchPaths([str(ASSETS)])
        self.viewer.setOpenExternalLinks(False)
        self.viewer.setOpenLinks(False)
        self.viewer.setFont(BODY_FONT)
        self.viewer.document().setDefaultFont(BODY_FONT)
        self.viewer.document().setDefaultStyleSheet(DOCUMENT_STYLE)
        self.viewer.setWordWrapMode(QTextOption.WrapMode.WrapAtWordBoundaryOrAnywhere)
        self.demo = QWidget()
        demo_layout = QHBoxLayout(self.demo)
        demo_layout.setContentsMargins(0, 0, 0, 0)
        demo_layout.setSpacing(12)
        label = QLabel('Illustration:')
        label.setFont(UI_FONT)
        demo_layout.addWidget(label)
        self.layer_buttons = QButtonGroup(self)
        for count in (1, 2, 3):
            button = QPushButton('%d layer%s' % (count, '' if count == 1 else 's'))
            button.setCheckable(True)
            button.setChecked(count == 1)
            button.setMinimumHeight(40)
            button.setFont(UI_FONT)
            button.setAccessibleName('Illustrate %d GPG layer%s' % (count, '' if count == 1 else 's'))
            button.setToolTip('Diagram only. Does not open files or perform encryption.')
            self.layer_buttons.addButton(button, count)
            demo_layout.addWidget(button)
        demo_layout.addStretch(1)
        self.layer_buttons.idClicked.connect(self.choose_layers)
        self.demo.hide()
        reader = QVBoxLayout()
        reader.setSpacing(12)
        reader.addWidget(self.demo)
        reader.addWidget(self.viewer, 1)
        body.addWidget(self.nav)
        body.addLayout(reader, 1)
        outer.addLayout(body, 1)
        self.nav.currentRowChanged.connect(self.select_section)
        self.section_picker.currentIndexChanged.connect(self.nav.setCurrentRow)
        close = QPushButton('Close')
        close.setFont(UI_FONT)
        close.clicked.connect(self.close)
        outer.addWidget(close, alignment=Qt.AlignRight)
        self.nav.setCurrentRow(0)

    def select_section(self, row):
        if row < 0:
            return
        self.section_picker.setCurrentIndex(row)
        self.demo.setVisible(list(SECTIONS)[row] == 'Encryption security levels')
        self._render_timer.start(0)

    def choose_layers(self, count):
        self.layer_count = count
        self.viewer.verticalScrollBar().setValue(0)
        self._render_timer.start(0)

    def resizeEvent(self, event):
        super().resizeEvent(event)
        if hasattr(self, 'nav'):
            compact = self.width() < 1000
            self.nav.setVisible(not compact)
            self.section_picker.setVisible(compact)
            self._render_timer.start(40)

    def fit_chapter_labels(self):
        # Adding the shared Node icons reduces the text column. Constrain each
        # item to the real viewport and measure wrapped labels instead of letting
        # the longest label create a hidden horizontal scroll range.
        width = self.nav.viewport().width()
        metrics = QFontMetrics(self.nav.font())
        text_width = max(80, width - self.nav.iconSize().width() - 40)
        for row in range(self.nav.count()):
            item = self.nav.item(row)
            bounds = metrics.boundingRect(QRect(0, 0, text_width, 1000), Qt.TextWordWrap, item.text())
            size = QSize(width, max(self.nav.iconSize().height(), bounds.height()) + 20)
            if item.sizeHint() != size:
                item.setSizeHint(size)

    def eventFilter(self, watched, event):
        # Reflow when the vertical scrollbar changes the available reading width.
        if watched in (self.viewer.viewport(), self.nav.viewport()) and event.type() == QEvent.Type.Resize:
            self._render_timer.start(40)
        return super().eventFilter(watched, event)

    def render_section(self):
        self.fit_chapter_labels()
        row = self.nav.currentRow()
        if row < 0:
            return
        section = list(SECTIONS)[row]
        # Vector commands are rendered at display size and device scale;
        # labels reflow instead of shrinking when the window gets narrower.
        available = int(self.viewer.viewport().width() - 2 * self.viewer.document().documentMargin() - 4)
        width = min(960, max(490, available))
        key = (section, width, self.layer_count, self.devicePixelRatioF())
        if key == self.render_key:
            return
        scroll = self.viewer.verticalScrollBar().value() if self.render_key and self.render_key[0] == section else 0
        svg, width, height, title, description, image = render_visual(
            section, width, self.layer_count, self.devicePixelRatioF())
        resource = QUrl('vault-guide:illustration')
        self.viewer.document().addResource(QTextDocument.ResourceType.ImageResource, resource, image)
        source = SECTIONS[section]
        split = source.index('</h2>') + len('</h2>')
        figure = ('<h3>' + escape(title) + '</h3>'
                  '<p style="line-height:100%;margin-bottom:16px"><img src="vault-guide:illustration" width="' + str(width) +
                  '" height="' + str(height) + '" alt="' + escape(description, quote=True) + '"></p>'
                  '<p style="color:#c4c4c4;margin-bottom:24px">' + escape(description) + '</p>')
        content = source[:split] + figure + source[split:]
        if section == 'Encryption security levels':
            _, cw, ch, comparison_description, comparison = render_comparison(width, self.devicePixelRatioF())
            self.viewer.document().addResource(QTextDocument.ResourceType.ImageResource,
                QUrl('vault-guide:comparison'), comparison)
            heading = '<h3>Multiple GPG layers are not multisig</h3>'
            comparison_html = ('<p style="line-height:100%;margin-bottom:16px"><img src="vault-guide:comparison" '
                'width="' + str(cw) + '" height="' + str(ch) + '" alt="' + escape(comparison_description, quote=True) + '"></p>'
                '<p style="color:#c4c4c4;margin-bottom:24px">' + escape(comparison_description) + '</p>')
            content = content.replace(heading, heading + comparison_html, 1)
        self.viewer.setHtml(content)
        for frame in self.viewer.document().rootFrame().childFrames():
            if isinstance(frame, QTextTable):
                table_format = frame.format()
                table_format.setTopMargin(16)
                table_format.setBottomMargin(24)
                frame.setFormat(table_format)
        self.viewer.verticalScrollBar().setValue(scroll)
        self.render_key = key
        self.current_svg = svg
        self.current_description = description


def main():
    app = QApplication(sys.argv)
    app.setStyle('Fusion')
    QIcon.setThemeName('Adwaita')
    QIcon.setFallbackThemeName('hicolor')
    app.setFont(UI_FONT)
    window = Guide()
    window.show()
    return app.exec()


if __name__ == '__main__':
    sys.exit(main())
